      "headline": "Software engineer and technology leader",
      "about": "I build software and the teams that build software.Over two decades of turning complex problems into working code. Started as the person who'd take on any task - from architecture to support tickets - because shipping matters more than ego. Still that person, just with a fancier title now.Spent time in the executive suite at Redbubble and Buildkite as CTO, learned a lot, but there's something about being closer to the work that just hits different. Currently back at Redbubble leading an engineering team, and getting my hands dirty with code again - turns out I missed it. What I actually do: I build teams that ship reliable software without burning out. I've learned that the best architecture is usually the boring one that everyone understands. I write code when it matters. I delete more code than I write when that matters more.I have:* Led engineering teams through scale-up chaos* Built CI/CD infrastructure that developers don't hate* Mentored enough engineers to know that the best thing you can teach someone is when to push back* Made enough mistakes to have strong opinions, loosely heldBased in Melbourne. Loving the engineering leadership role right now, but I've done the C-suite thing and would do it again for something compelling.If you want to work together or just talk shop, reach out. If you're recruiting, please read my experience first - I promise it'll save us both time.",
